#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:5
#: a0dcaba58362472ba0cc06e8387b22b5
msgid "CRUISE Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:7
#: 990a3a46431b42f99dc0ac05d5104504
msgid "Cruise mode is a bit like :ref:`FLY BY WIRE_B (FBWB) <fbwb-mode>`, but it has \"heading lock\". It is the ideal mode for longer distance FPV flight, as you can point the plane at a distant object and it will accurately track to that object, automatically controlling altitude, airspeed and heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:15
#: a296e23a602440ea96225e70acc63e1c
msgid "CRUISE mode is not suitable for flight close to the ground. The time constants for height control in CRUISE mode are the ones from TECS, which are quite slow. When you are close to the ground CRUISE mode does not give you the agility needed in pitch control to avoid hitting the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:21
#: 61b69c6cf88a4a6888c4222139f7820c
msgid "The way it works is this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:23
#: 53cbed254bc34d888c6cf68765cd769d
msgid "if you have any aileron or rudder input then it flies just like :ref:`FBWB <fbwb-mode>`. So it holds altitude until you use the elevator to change the target altitude (at the ``FBWB_CLIMB_RATE`` rate) and it adjusts airspeed based on throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:27
#: 86cdc41ae1fc403b932ba3fc63baf129
msgid "when you let go of the aileron and rudder sticks for more than 0.5 seconds it sets an internal waypoint at your current location, and projects a target waypoint one kilometre ahead (note that heading lock will only activate if you have GPS lock, and have a ground speed of at least 3 m/s)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:32
#: cc0411b2561d411cbfb4875a5e71e5fb
msgid "as it flies along it heads for the target waypoint, and constantly updates that target to always be one kilometre ahead, leaving the previous waypoint as the position that you centred the aileron and rudder sticks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:36
#: 0440fa5cf58e4839b6a2119f8ae434fb
msgid "as long as you don't touch the aileron or rudder, it will run the same navigation system it uses for waypoints, including crabbing, cross-track etc, so it will very accurately hold that ground course even in the face of changing wind conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:41
#: e8cb7c9fc90d4c0fa2db73d4b4551ba7
msgid "One of the nicer aspects of CRUISE mode is how it handles rudder. If you give it some rudder then the roll controller will keep the wings level, but the plane will yaw with the rudder. So you get a \"wings level\" turn, allowing you to rotate your flight to point at whatever geographic feature you want to head towards. Then when you let go of the rudder it will head straight for that point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:48
#: 29d60898e1f141b6b34d3b1611b18609
msgid "Note that you can configure CRUISE mode to do terrain following on autopilots with microSD storage available. See the :ref:`terrain following documentation <common-terrain-following>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cruise-mode.rst:54
#: be3e3b10e90a4c4c843cea284c0f1890
msgid "Make sure you only fly FPV if it is allowed by your country's flight and airspace control rules. Many countries do not allow non-line-of-sight flight without a special operating license."
msgstr ""

